  {
    "question_id": "Q11.5",
    "class": 7,
    "subject": "science",
    "chapter_number": 11,
    "chapter_name": "transportation in animals and plants",
    "question_type": "conceptual",
    "question_text": "Why is transport of materials necessary in a plant or in an animal? Explain.",
    "question_latex": null,
    "mcq_options": [],
    "correct_option": null,
    "question_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "Transport of materials is necessary in both plants and animals as every cell needs a regular supply of nutrients and oxygen for releasing energy through respiration. The food that we eat is broken down into smaller components to be absorbed by the cells. The oxygen that we inhale is also transported to all the cells of the body. Our body also requires a constant removal of waste materials such as carbon dioxide. For the transport of all these materials (food, oxygen, and wastes), our body has a specialised transport system. Similarly, in plants, the transport of water and food is accomplished with the help of a complex transport system.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Thus, transport is essential for survival and functioning of both plants and animals.",
    "answer_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "difficulty_rating": 3,
    "difficulty_reasoning": "Requires understanding of biological processes and systems.",
    "topics_tags": [
      "Transport in Plants",
      "Transport in Animals",
      "Biological Systems"
    ],
    "confidence_score": 0.95,
    "confidence_issues": [],
    "question_images": [],
    "answer_images": []
