  {
    "question_id": "Q11.9",
    "class": 7,
    "subject": "science",
    "chapter_number": 11,
    "chapter_name": "transportation in animals and plants",
    "question_type": "conceptual",
    "question_text": "What are the components of blood?",
    "question_latex": null,
    "mcq_options": [],
    "correct_option": null,
    "question_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "The main components of blood are:\n(i) Red blood cells (RBCs): Red blood cells are the most abundant cells in the blood. These cells contain a red pigment called haemoglobin. It is the haemoglobin which carries oxygen and transports it to all parts of the body.\n(ii) White blood cells (WBCs): WBCs are colourless cells without haemoglobin. They fight against infections and protect the body from foreign particles such as germs and bacteria.\n(iii) Platelets: Platelets are the smallest cells in the blood. The main function of platelet is to prevent bleeding.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Thus, blood consists of RBCs, WBCs, and platelets, each serving vital functions.",
    "answer_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
